3.29.m:
The diverse Śaktis, constantly eager for the slaying of the Asura Bhaṇḍa, [advanced];
yet even that circular doorway, extending a yojana in length and width,
was not sufficient for the commander of the army of the fire-rampart circle.

Because of the speed and dexterity of her hand, nothing could be discerned
of the movement of the Mahārājñī’s lotus-hand in discharging arrows;
listen, O pot-born [Agastya], I shall tell you all about the combat.
